WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our next guest is
a wonderful actress

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.537
who earned an Emmy nomination
for her role as Shiv Roy

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.738
on the hit series "Succession."

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.407
The highly-anticipated
third season premieres

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:11.210
Sunday, October 17th on HBO
and to stream on HBO Max.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.411
Here's a clip.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:14.013
Oh, right.
They wouldn't send one.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.083
[ Laughing ]

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.918
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.286
and to the studio
for the first time,

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:21.387
Sarah Snook!

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.156
[ Applause ]

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:30.196 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:37.270 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.406
-I am delighted to have you
here in person.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.707
-Yeah. It's good to be here.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.844
-I got to have you --
we Zoomed over the pandemic,

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.978
but this is so much nicer.

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:49.549
-Yeah, absolutely.
-Yeah. It's real life.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.783
-It's still unnerving,
but it's in real life.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.452
-Also nice to have you back
in New York City,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.287
and I know you sort of
came from Australia to do press

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.355
and we were talking backstage --

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.256
you will basically have to
quarantine

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.291
when you get back to Australia
for as long as you were here.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:00.393
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.228
-Yeah, which is why
this is unnerving.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.429
Being in person with anybody
right now.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:04.697
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.865
They're like, "Were you anywhere
with a bunch of people?"

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.199
And you're like, "Uh..."

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:09.636
-There's no evidence anywhere.
Don't worry about it.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.705
-You spent some time
living in Brooklyn, yeah?

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.474
-Yeah.
-Did you like it?

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.774
-I love it. I love Brooklyn.

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:17.810
It's like...I don't know,
Brooklyn's like --

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.011
[ Applause ]
-Yeah, right?

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:20.713
It's great. I don't know.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:24.350
Brooklyn's like, the fighty,
little brother to Manhattan

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.086
or like
the Australia to America.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.520
It's like,
on the outside looking in,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.587
but you get the better view.

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.423
-Do you think that you --

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.525
do you find everything is
sibling rivalries

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.093
now that you're on "Succession"?

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.528
-Yeah, I mean, weirdly,

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.130
I don't have much of a sibling
rivalry with my sisters, though,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.398
so I guess so, I do.

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:40.499
-Are you the youngest of three?

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:41.500
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.804
You know, I'm wondering --

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.306
one of the things that's so much
fun watching you guys as actors,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.676
it's very clear that you
like each other.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:54.013
Mostly because you are
being definitely mean to

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.682
people that in real life,
you care about.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.049
-Yes.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.617
-Is there anyone you like
being mean to the most?

00:01:58.617 --> 00:01:59.619
-Kieran.
-Kieran.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.920
-Totally.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.256
-I was gonna say, I've met
Kieran and he's lovely,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.690
but I think he'd be super fun
to be mean to.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.560
-Oh, yeah, but he's also
super mean to just to be fun,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.794
you know, like, to you.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:10.730
-Right.
-That's the way he shows love.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.831
-Is it true that you guys
early on,

00:02:12.831 --> 00:02:14.500
before you knew each other well,
had to be, like,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.834
physical in a scene together?

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:19.672
-Yeah, well, we had to fight --
like, wrestle, and yeah.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.807
I mean, this was like,
the first episode back

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:25.010
in the first season shooting
and we had to wrestle,

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.580
and we tried -- you know,
the stunt coordinator's there

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.915
and he's like, teaching us
how to do it properly

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:31.684
so we don't hurt each other,
and then finally, Kieran's like,

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.419
"Can I just slap you?
It's gonna be easier."

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.355
I was like, "Okay, sure.
For this one, fine."

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:39.191
And he slaps me, and there's
a sibling kick that happened,

00:02:39.191 --> 00:02:40.459
and I just went for him.

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.296
And then he knows WWE
for some reason.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.897
He's a tiny, little wrestler.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.332
He's just obsessed
with watching it.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.767
And he just knew how to
do all the holds,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.001
so I thought I was winning
for awhile,

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.103
but then, like,
he got me up against the wall

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:53.039
and like, pulled me down.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.640
-And then when you watched it,
did you realize,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.042
"Oh, that's the take they used,
when we fully went for it."

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.476
-Yeah, 100%. Yeah.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:58.678
Because you can see in my eyes,
like,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:02.482
there's some little thing
that goes, "Oh, [bleep]."

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.116
It's like a little fly swat
or something.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.618
"Get away from me."

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.687
-Do you ever,
when you have time off --

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.823
like, I know you had a big,
obviously layoff during COVID.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:11.991
Do you try to
come up with things

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:13.492
that you think Shiv would say?

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:14.794
Like, Shiv terminology?

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.895
-Yeah. The thing is, though...

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:18.764
I mean, I found this word,
"yoga babble."

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:19.798
Have you heard that?

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:21.033
-Yoga babble? No.
-Yeah, yoga babble.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.868
Yoga babble's like
the encompassing word

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.004
for bull[bleep], I guess.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.940
It's like,
business world bull[bleep].

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.143
But I feel like anything in
business is yoga babble to me,

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.411
in a little way.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.679
I feel like Business Cat when
I'm learning about

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:34.813
all the business things.

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:36.716
You know,
mergers and all this stuff.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.184
I'm like the business cat
who does this.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.518
You know that gif
just doing this?

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.921
-You're the extra in
the background at a computer.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.255
-Business business business.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:45.124
You don't do this anymore.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.193
It's laptops here.
-You're very convincing.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.360
You're very convincing
as someone who,

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.662
it's becoming clear now,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.097
knows nothing about
the character you're playing.

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:54.467
-I'm an actor.
I just do what I'm told.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.935
-Matthew MacFadyen,
your wonderful costar,

00:03:56.935 --> 00:03:59.739
was here yesterday, and
I asked him about Brian Cox.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.507
I'm fascinated by Brian Cox,
who I've never met.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.310
I said, "He seems irascible,
but I'm sure he's sweet."

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.411
What's your answer to that?

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.846
-The same. Exactly.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.248
He's irascible. No, he's lovely.
He's a big teddy bear.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:12.952
He loves, you know, being
loud and rambunctious.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:16.055
-We had to blur his face mask,
because this is what he wore

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.122
to the premiere last night.

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:18.991
It's #TeamLoganRoy,

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.827
and see if you guys can guess
what's blurred out.

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:23.929
[ Laughing ]

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:25.964
-Just so you can understand
what he was about to say.

00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:27.300
-Yep.
-Through the mask.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.401
-Nominated for an Emmy,
but I heard

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:31.970
you won another prestigious
award that I was unaware of.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.205
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:34.974
-The Meryl Streep Acting Award.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.175
-Yeah. Did you know about this?
-I didn't know about --

00:04:37.175 --> 00:04:38.711
-When I was 11? What?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.046
-Okay, so you're 11 years old.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.647
Who gave out
the Meryl Streep Acting Award?

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:45.118
-My Year 6 teacher, Mr. Cornish.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:47.553
I mean, he gave awards
to everybody.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.455
Everybody in the class
got an award,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.190
and I just happened to get
the Meryl Streep Award,

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:54.026
because I was really the loudest
and more performative one.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:56.361
I mean, I'm sure that
there was an Einstein Award,

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:57.763
and I'm sure there was --

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.232
-Now, did you know at the time
this was not a real award?

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:03.102
Or did you go off to Year 7
being like,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.204
"Make way for the Meryl Streep
winner."

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.740
-The queen is here.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.241
Yeah, definitely.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.077
Yeah, I took that home.
I still have it somewhere.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.212
It's like,
in my collection of stuff.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.314
-As well you should. You don't
get rid of something like that.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:16.749
-No, I mean,
it was made on wood,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.718
and I'm sure there was that
paperclip on there somewhere,

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.586
but it's still in my stuff.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.855
-We talked about how people
were very taken with Shiv

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.790
as well as Shiv's look.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.859
You know, she has a very
unique fashion sense

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.360
which I think people
were drawn to,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.029
because they
love the show so much.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.964
Halloween's coming around.
You have seen, right?

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.733
You have seen people dress up
like Shiv for Halloween.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.534
-I have, yeah.
-That's really high praise.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:39.071
-Yeah, but isn't it the easiest
Halloween costume ever?

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:41.673
It's just donning a red wig,
bob sort of thing

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:43.642
and putting on a turtleneck
and high-waisted pants.

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:45.911
I mean, I've got the red hair,

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:48.114
but I can't wear turtlenecks
or high-waisted pants anywhere,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.882
'cause I look like I'm
a Halloween costume.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:53.920
-That would be like an athlete
wearing his uniform out.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.320
-Yeah.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.425
-Hey, can I do -- I have
a really good Kendall Roy.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:00.860
Can I do it for you?
-Oh, yes.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.294
-Okay great. Okay.

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:04.697
[ As Kendall Roy ] Uh...

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.598
Dad?

00:06:06.598 --> 00:06:08.634
-Very good.
-Thank you.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.369
-Very good.

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.138
That's like, wow.

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.507
It was the spirit. Yeah,
the spirit was in the room.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.075
Yeah, it was the pause.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:18.077
-You must be so psyched

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:19.645
that people get to
see the show again.

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.013
I mean, we were so --
I think everybody,

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.548
after the cliffhanger of
Season 2,

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:25.217
was chomping at the bit
to see it again.

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:27.286
Do you feel great excitement
that the rest of the world

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.320
gets to see what you've done?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.622
-Oh, yeah, totally.

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:32.091
And also, the anticipation
that I've been feeling,

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.527
from between working,
being shut down

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:35.661
and then waiting to work
and like,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.829
wanting to know
what happens next,

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.530
finally getting to know
what happens next.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.433
I know that anticipation,
so I sympathize.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:43.869
And getting to see the episodes
finally, myself,

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:45.437
it's like -- I'm a big fan
of the show as well,

00:06:45.437 --> 00:06:47.773
because we don't get to
see what Greg and Tom does.

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:49.007
Or we don't get to see

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:52.244
what Brian's doing with
all the other scenes.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:53.879
I love getting to watch the show
as well.

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:55.047
-That's great.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.582
I'm so excited
and I just want to tell you

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:57.783
this is a big deal for us.

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:59.185
You're the first
Meryl Streep winner

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:01.553
ever to be here.

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:04.022
And maybe even last.

00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:05.158
-Maybe.
-Unless you come back,

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:06.525
which we would love to
have you back.

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:08.293
You guys, Sarah Snook!

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:10.196
"Succession" returns
for its third season

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:13.232
October 17th on HBO
and to stream on HBO Max.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.867
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

